 #edb/ref 17592186069674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068939 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068939 #edb/ref 1050 480.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068939 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "045e390c-f9e0-5c62-a1d5-1f73b3832910" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069674 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069674 #edb/ref 1061 193672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069674 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c8c690e8-98b4-5d35-95ce-fc393db9c622" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069674 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069675 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069675 #edb/ref 1061 193673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069675 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e0a72e00-797b-57f4-a45c-96e085feac0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069675 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069676 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069676 #edb/ref 1061 193677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069676 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b17aa434-a47c-53cc-81b8-1a470742a699" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069676 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069677 #edb/ref 1061 193680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069677 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "99fc25d8-4973-51af-b980-015f39c45ced" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069677 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070037 #edb/ref 1064 "To solve a two-term quadratic equation like $x^2 - 7x = 0$ where there is no constant term, we can factor out the variable and apply the zero-product rule.\n\nFactoring out the variable, we have:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\tx^2 - 7x &= 0 \\\n\tx(x - 7) &= 0\n}\n$$\n\nWe apply the zero product rule to get \n\n$$\nx=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad x-7=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives \n\n$$\nx=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad x=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=0,7.$\n\nTo check that these solutions are correct, we can substitute them back into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =0 & \\, & \\, & x & =7 \\\\  & ⇓ &  &  &  & ⇓ \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x & =0 &  &  & {x}^{2}-7x & =0 \\\\ {0}^{2}-7(0) & =0 &  &  & {7}^{2}-7(7) & =0 \\\\ 0-0 & =0 &  &  & 49-49 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓ &  &  & 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Warning:** It's tempting to solve the equation by dividing by $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-7x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-7x}{x} & =\\frac{0}{x} \\\\ x-7 & =0 \\\\ x & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, if we do that, we lose the solution $x=0.$ So, when solving equations, *never divide by a variable* because the variable could be zero, and division by zero is not allowed. Instead, try to factor the variable in the equation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070037 #edb/ref 1065 9238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070037 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "bda6c872-00e7-50b0-b4bb-685694b60283" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070037 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186544897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186544907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186544984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Quadratic Equations with No Constant Term" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186544907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544082 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e36e2817-44dd-5f9f-b222-4aa63a5581d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544274 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544274 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544274 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5468f005-5491-5c41-9fe4-04