ef 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557176 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557176 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186556525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557176 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c2c3da63-61c2-5820-b9db-e69f9530157d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557212 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $4{g}^{2}=\\frac{2g}{5}$ are $g=${{field-1}} and $g=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d0ef510-de0c-500a-8eb5-ba614cc6f88f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557212 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{g}^{2} & =\\frac{2g}{5} \\\\ 4{g}^{2}-\\frac{2g}{5} & =0 \\\\ 2g(2g-\\frac{1}{5}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\n2g=0\\,\\text{or}\\,2g-\\frac{1}{5}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\ng=0\\,\\text{or}\\,g=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $g=0$ and $g=\\frac{1}{10}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557221 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557221 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557221 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223742" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557221 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557221 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $\\frac{1}{5}{t}^{2}=-3t$ are $t=${{field-1}} and $t=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557221 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "267a0513-367c-516d-9933-b0be78b78e58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557221 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{t}^{2} & =-3t \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}{t}^{2}+3t & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}t(t+15) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}t=0\\,\\text{or}\\,t+15=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nt=0\\,\\text{or}\\,t=-15.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $t=-15$ and $t=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557223 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557223 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557223 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557223 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $6{w}^{2}+3w-5=2{w}^{2}-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557223 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "27e28aad-c990-5820-b03a-4018644801a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557223 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{w}^{2}+3w-5 & =2{w}^{2}-5 \\\\ 6{w}^{2}+3w-5-(2{w}^{2}-5) & =0 \\\\ 6{w}^{2}+3w-5-2{w}^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ (6{w}^{2}-2{w}^{2})+3w+(-5+5) & =0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}+3w & =0 \\\\ w(4w+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\nw=0\\,\\text{or}\\,4w+3=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nw=0\\,\\text{or}\\,w=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $w=-\\frac{3}{4},0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557342 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "13841e88-b264-587e-a3ba-4dee503e95bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557342 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186557212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557352 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186557342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557352 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3cfceae3-a898-59b0-bb61-c360e1ebdc6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557352 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186557221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557363 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186557352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557363 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "679c8709-10da-518a-990d-837568e38654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557363 #e